# .dockerignore, FraudLens Week 12. Keeps the Docker build context to just
# what the image actually needs (requirements.txt, src/), the same
# "only what is actually used" discipline requirements.txt itself follows.
#
# Trained model artifacts, the MLflow/audit SQLite files, and raw/
# generated data are excluded on purpose, not by oversight: they are this
# project's DATA, bind-mounted in at container start by docker-compose.yml
# rather than baked into the image. See Dockerfile's own comment on this.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.gitignore
data/
mlruns/
models/
mlflow.db
audit_log.db
tests/
*.md
.venv/
venv/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
